      "claim": "Every clause that could displace POL-NS-03 instead points straight at it. POL-NS-01 cannot keep this fee alive: limb (b) fails because the trace holds zero qualifying in-radius fixes, and limb (d) fails because the trip was terminated by the driver with cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, which POL-NS-01 expressly excludes and routes to POL-NS-03. POL-NS-05 does not catch this driver either - he was stationary within 300 m of the pin (284.95 m) when the arrival marker was set at 15:12:05 - and POL-NS-05 itself hands a driver stationary within 300 m but outside the radius to POL-NS-03. POL-NS-01 limb (b) failing is exactly the state POL-NS-03 is drafted to resolve.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00206 at weight_multiplier 0.8 but does not name its issue code(s): LOW_SAMPLE_RATE"
    },
    {
      "claim": "POL-NS-06 does not strip the driver's goodwill. POL-NS-06 addresses the driver who never held position where he could be met, and whose in-geofence dwell fell short; this driver did hold, stationary and within 400 m of the pin, for the full required dwell. POL-NS-03 is the specific clause for the wrong-entrance fact pattern - it is where POL-NS-01 and POL-NS-02 both send a DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE trip - and it fixes compensation for exactly this contingency, governing 'the outcome including the driver's compensation'. A general shortfall clause does not swallow the specific provision the code routes to.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00206 at weight_multiplier 0.8 but does not name its issue code(s): LOW_SAMPLE_RATE"
