    "explanation": "To the rider: your $4.00 cancellation fee is refunded in full. To the driver: you receive a $2.00 platform-funded goodwill payment, and it is not taken out of the rider's refund.\n\nWhy the fee is refunded. POL-NS-01 lets a no-show fee stand only if four conditions hold. Two fail here. The trip was ended by the driver with the code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE — POL-NS-01 treats that code as the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider, expressly excludes it from the chargeable codes (limb (d)), and routes the trip to POL-NS-03. And the GPS trace never brings the driver inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius: his closest approach was 284.95 m and the count of qualifying in-radius fixes is 0 (limb (b)). The fee is therefore not chargeable.\n\nWhere the driver stands. The driver did hold position — stationary for roughly 400 seconds (trip_record.wait_time_min is 6.6) at about 285 m from the pin. That is outside the 120 m arrival radius but inside the 400 m wrong-entrance ceiling POL-NS-03 sets, so POL-NS-03 governs, as POL-NS-01 and POL-NS-02 both direct and as POL-NS-05 confirms by handing a driver stationary within 300 m of the pin to it. Allocating fault from the chat log alone, as POL-NS-03 requires, neither party named an entrance, block, tower or bay — it holds two SYSTEM notifications only — and the trip record shows 4 registered pickup points at this LARGE_VENUE. POL-NS-03(ii) therefore attributes the mis-location to pin ambiguity rather than to either party, and pays the driver 50 percent of the $4.00 cancellation fee = $2.00, funded by the platform and never recovered from the rider. The rider's $4.00 refund and the driver's $2.00 are independent and are not netted.\n\nThe other clauses. POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06 both also produce a full refund (the trace shows 0 seconds of in-geofence dwell against the 300 second minimum), but POL-NS-03 is the specific clause the code routes a DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE trip to, and it is the clause that fixes the driver's compensation, so it governs that question. POL-NS-04 does not apply: it needs a locating or coordinating message from the rider in the chat log, and there is none. POL-NS-05 does not catch this arrival marker, because the driver was within 300 m of the pin, so no false-arrival referral is recorded. POL-NS-07 gives the driver no fee-funded 80 percent payment, because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied, and its anti-farming check does not trip (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d = 1, below 4; 1/187 = 0.005, far below 0.08).\n\nNo escalation. Confidence is 0.80, above the 0.70 floor. The fare reconciles: $4.00 equals the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee ($4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee ($4.00), so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged. rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 and both parties' disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0, so POL-NS-09(c) and (d) are not engaged, and no deciding fact rests solely on evidence impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d).\n\nEvidence and confidence. The deciding fact — the driver's position — is carried by EV-GPS-00206, which is impaired at weight_multiplier 0.8 for issue LOW_SAMPLE_RATE (median 18 s sampling against a nominal 10 s cadence). That impairment is schema-level only, not policy-level: the largest gap is 26 s (well under POL-NS-08(b)'s 120 s), the trace holds 52 fixes and it does carry the rider track, so POL-NS-08 is not engaged and the ruling is not capped at PARTIAL_REFUND. It discounts confidence under POL-GEN-02(2), which is why confidence is 0.80, the weight of that artifact. The finding survives the discount, because every fix the trace does carry places the driver far outside the 120 m radius. EV-CHAT-00206, EV-TRIP-00206 and EV-FARE-00206 carry their facts at weight 1.0."
